      "op": "note",
      "text": "The Stargate dialer (D1, docs/pending/SWITCHBOARD.md 'Stargate dialer'). Day 1: a call (the traveller decided correctly; if denied, the board's call as an approval makes it), D turns to the board, the ring turns the nation under the top chevron (seq ring_place) and the era under chevron 2 (seq ring_era), cells carried to the mark (seq cell_seat), MASTER thrown (seq master), the 20 s calibration (seq strobe; a still at about 10 s), '+1 SENT'. Then a wrong era pops the fuse and one drag fixes it. Day 5: 3 dials and the rack. A right-click lets go of a held ring, the next backs out (then a still of the board on the wall); Esc lets go of a held ring, the next closes the board (on this base Esc opens Settings on the PC, D20 and R3; D13's back-out lands with cheats-fix). Stills at 16:9, 5:4 and 21:9. board_day1.tsv logs every frame's ring turn, lenses and bars."
